#
# hrx-system commit the daily bump-hrx run must not move away from. While a commit is named
# here, bump-hrx does not merge AMD's hrx-system pin into 1bit-MONSTER/hrx-system 1bit/main,
# keeps third_party/hrx-system where it is, and takes only AMD's llama.cpp changes outside the
# HRX backend (AMD's ggml-hrx is written against AMD's hrx-system). Delete the commit line to
# lift the hold.
#
# Held 2026-10-10 by the owner: the engine stays on our HRX line. AMD's hrx-system after
# 98d05d94 carries the long-context attention miscompile from ba07714dd (ROCm/hrx-system#1535),
# and the move also needs the loom-jit.cpp port (llama.cpp fork #97) and the kernel corpus
# rename to `multiple_of`. Two of those three reasons were measured on 2026-10-15/16: the
# loom-jit.cpp LoomC port landed in llama.cpp `ad18320a` (and the merged `hrx-pins-guard`
# workflow now checks it), and the corpus rename is only needed for AMD's renamed revision -
# `1bit-MONSTER/hrx-system` `1bit/main` still accepts `mul`, and so does 98d05d94. The #1535
# long-context question is the one that remains open, which is why this file still names a
# commit rather than being emptied.
#
# 2026-10-16, R1 backport (owner decision): the hold now names `1bit/held-98d05d94-3fixes`,
# a branch off the held pin carrying three verified fixes - engine#409 (libhrx bounds-checks a
# length-less ELF extent instead of skipping the check), engine#410 (libhip_intercept covers
# every HIP symbol the backend exports; env-var and double-init defects fixed) and engine#401
# (libhsa no longer opens /dev/accel in GPU-only processes) - plus the +61/-0 `api.h`
# forward-port the regenerated stubs need. The held AMD core is unchanged, so the #1535
# question stays exactly where it was. The durable move is still to rebase these fixes onto
# our line (or lift the hold) once the long-prompt check passes there; this line exists so
# three small fixes do not have to wait for that.
# 2026-10-18, owner decision: the engine moves to AMD's e3e6a9766ccb with our commits replayed
# on it (fork branch `1bit/e3e6a976-pin`): HRX_AQL_BLOCK_SIZE/HRX_COMMAND_BUFFER_MODE, the
# engine#409, #410 and #401 fixes, and our fix for ROCm/hrx-system#1535 (AMD's multi-unit
# live-out guard is still in unit_liveness_builder.c, so we keep removing it). The pin is a
# `-s ours` merge of 3319e536 whose tree is the tested commit fc2213a1c exactly. Measured
# 2026-10-17 on strixhalo against the old pin: test-backend-ops 1141/1141 x3, needle 7341 @4732
# 20/20, @4432 5/5, Qwen3-1.7B 5/5, KLD 0 on Qwen3-0.6B and ZAYA1-8B, +3-8 % pp/tg. The hold
# stays, now naming that commit, so the daily run does not take AMD's later hrx-system (or its
# ggml-hrx) without the same checks.
